{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: bare counts of small discrete foods with no piece weight",
  "description": "Lines that count a food USDA doesn't weigh by the piece give \"Unsupported quantity unit\". \
Done: nuts (cashews 1.5 g, pecan and walnut halves 1.5 and 2.0 g, from FNDDS's '1 nut'), hot dogs (52 g) and smoked sausage links (68 g) from SR Legacy, and candy that SR weighs by the piece (caramels 10.1 g, gummy worms 7.4 g, fun-size Butterfingers 18 g). `make ingredient-catalog-audit` writes every failure line to logs/ingredient-catalog-failures.json for before/after diffs. \
Remaining, grouped: candy USDA doesn't weigh by its piece (\"2/4 candy canes\": SR's hard candy piece is 6 g, a cane is more; \"10 jujubees\" resolves to the jujube fruit); dried currants (\"12 dried currants or raisins\" resolves to currants, which have no piece; FNDDS's 0.5 g is labeled a slice/chunk); olives and pickles (\"16 kalamata or other black olives\", \"6 to 7 pitted kalamata olives\", \"6 pepperoncini\", \"1 umeboshi\" x3, \"3 marinated artichoke hearts\" x3, \"3/4 canned artichokes\", \"2 jarred roasted red peppers\", \"1 roasted red pepper\"); counted whole spices (\"12 pods green cardamom\", \"24 whole cloves\": more than MAX_TRACE_COUNT, so they need a cited piece weight or a higher cap for tiny pieces); citrus peel (\"3/4 strips lemon zest\", \"2 lemon twists\", \"1 orange peel\", \"1 piece lemon/orange peel\"); pasta and bread pieces (\"20 / 25-30 jumbo dried pasta shells\", \"6/4 whole wheat tortillas\", \"24 1/4-inch-thick baguette bread slices\" x3 and \"24 baguette slices or rye cocktail bread\" (a baguette slice is not French bread's 64 g slice), \"12 to 16 1-inch thick rounds French bread\", \"16 sourdough toast fingers\" x3, \"2 piece sourdough or whole grain bread\" x3, \"2 piece toasted bread\"); \"12-15 thin slices pancetta\"; \"2 layers sliced cheddar\" x3; \"12-15 green peas\", \"4 piece salmon fillets\", \"6-7 piece shrimp\", \"1 piece thick-cut bacon\", \"1 boneless rib eye steak\", \"1/0.25 Japanese leek\". \
Take whole sub-groups with cited per-piece weights (the USDA FDC CSV archives that scripts/import-catalog.py downloads have every portion row, including counts the catalog import drops; USDA Branded labels give counts per serving for most packaged foods). \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (and logs/ingredient-catalog-failures.json); make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
